# Marker: FuseSoC's library scanner (and Booley's discover_cores) skip any
# directory carrying this file. .booley_project/ holds transient git
# worktrees whose .core copies share the project's VLNV — without this
# marker FuseSoC's recursive --cores-root scan would let a stale worktree
# core shadow the repo-root source and silently build the wrong RTL.
#
# One subtree is exempt BY DESIGN: cores/ (stealth authored cores, ADR
# 0036). Booley scans it as a second root, so this marker never applies
# to it — do not drop a FUSESOC_IGNORE inside cores/ unless you mean to
# hide those cores from Booley too.
